I also tightened v8 beyond v7:
full 9,984-expert routing + gradient screen per capability;
hierarchical causal search over the top 8 causal layers, with four randomized searches;
48 independently sampled population experts per capability;
score-selected sentinels kept separate from population correlations;
exact causal + renormalized causal measurements;
precise FP32 target/control gradient geometry;
matched adaptation atlas;
final selectors constructed from selection data only;
validation adaptation cannot choose the final selector;
untouched 25+25 final test;
3 training-order seeds for K=1 confirmation;
K=1/2/4/8 curves for causal, routing, gradient, and gradient-specific;
resumable global gradient, causal-layer, hierarchical, panel, adaptation, final, and budget phases;
exact Laguna newline teacher forcing retained;
exact-baseline delta surgery retained;
frozen BF16 base integrity checked after every arm.
I also fixed a subtle remaining issue from v7: after training, v8 now physically merges the trained FP32
expert masters back into Laguna's BF16 fused expert tensors and evaluates through Laguna's
native expert kernel. It then restores the original base tensors. Every training arm records:
delta_merge_max_nll_diff
and the final validity audit checks that the delta-vs-native-merge discrepancy stays below 0.01.
